ive-resolution-v15-6\",\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-4\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Earlier non-crashing completion-count obligations explicitly survive restart and remain subject to retained EOF auditing.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000007\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000005\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md\",\n      \"local_id\": \"53\",\n      \"decision\": \"represented\",\n      \"proposal_ids\": [\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-6\",\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-2\",\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-1\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Every scenario step must follow the preceding journal/UI rules, including permanent cancellation and irreversible grants.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000007\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000003\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000002\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md\",\n      \"local_id\": \"54\",\n      \"decision\": \"represented\",\n      \"proposal_ids\": [\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-6\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Statement and acceptance intent explicitly prohibit treating flow planning as scenario execution.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000007\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md\",\n      \"local_id\": \"55\",\n      \"decision\": \"represented\",\n      \"proposal_ids\": [\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-7\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Synthetic adapters are explicitly required implementation work, without any assertion that executable endpoints already exist.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000008\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md\",\n      \"local_id\": \"56\",\n      \"decision\": \"represented\",\n      \"proposal_ids\": [\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-7\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"The reward-controller implementer owns the explicit downstream handoff to select and document one shared versioned profile, including hook acknowledgement representation and return path.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000008\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md\",\n      \"local_id\": \"57\",\n      \"decision\": \"represented\",\n      \"proposal_ids\": [\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-7\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Encoding and argument spelling remain permitted design choices, while the downstream plan must resolve its selected profile. This bounded delegation does not leave the semantic proposal incomplete.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000008\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md\",\n      \"local_id\": \"58\",\n      \"decision\": \"represented\",\n      \"proposal_ids\": [\n        \"proposal:exclusive-resolution-v15-7\"\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"Every permitted profile must preserve all listed identities, distinctions, ordering, barriers, independent observations, retained counts, deadlines and scenarios.\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        {\n          \"span_ref\": \"span-000008\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_ids\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"find